WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.029
Option B joins the Grid to Universal DDI,

2
00:00:03.029 --> 00:00:06.550
Infoblox's software-as-a-service
control plane.

3
00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:09.908
You add a join token from the
Infoblox Portal to the Grid,

4
00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:13.412
then turn on IPAM Federation
and Cloud Grid Management.

5
00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:20.762
Federation, which needs NIOS 9.0.4 or later,
keeps address space unique everywhere.

6
00:00:20.762 --> 00:00:24.300
The Grid stays primary for its DNS data.

7
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.312
What does it add?

8
00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:30.750
It's the only documented Infoblox
mechanism that writes back to cloud DNS.

9
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:35.820
It syncs Route 53, Azure DNS
and Google Cloud DNS read-write,

10
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:41.312
and it discovers resolver endpoints
and rules in AWS and Azure.

11
00:00:41.312 --> 00:00:44.523
Cloud forwarders take
queries in from a cloud,

12
00:00:44.523 --> 00:00:47.650
and cloud to cloud only
between AWS and Azure.

13
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.287
And on commercial AWS,
Infoblox can be the outside

14
00:00:51.287 --> 00:00:55.812
authority for a VPC IPAM private
scope, on the Advanced Tier.

15
00:00:55.812 --> 00:00:57.449
The limits are documented.

16
00:00:57.449 --> 00:01:01.650
Route 53 sync doesn't support
non-simple routing policies.

17
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:05.225
Azure and Google private zones
can't be created from the portal.

18
00:01:05.225 --> 00:01:07.050
DNSSEC records aren't synced.

19
00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:11.697
And the portal can't promote a Grid
Master Candidate or manage DHCP failover,

20
00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:14.500
so the Grid Master stays
the recovery console.

21
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.650
Two more notes.

22
00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:20.586
The cloud forwarding and private-zone
features run on NIOS-X servers,

23
00:01:20.586 --> 00:01:24.050
not classic Trinzic, so
you'd need NIOS-X capacity.

24
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.729
And the government edition:
Infoblox Government Cloud

25
00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:31.488
is FedRAMP Certified at
Moderate, hosted in AWS GovCloud.

26
00:01:31.488 --> 00:01:37.125
Its cloud discovery is limited: single
AWS accounts and no Azure tenants.

27
00:01:37.125 --> 00:01:40.532
The VPC IPAM handoff isn't
in its release notes,

28
00:01:40.532 --> 00:01:44.025
and AWS excludes GovCloud
from that integration.

29
00:01:44.025 --> 00:01:46.075
Confirm the rest with Infoblox.

30
00:01:46.075 --> 00:01:51.260
Sources: Infoblox Onboarding NIOS
Services, NIOS Grid Connector,

31
00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:57.884
Managing NIOS from Infoblox Portal, Universal
DDI and NIOS Grid Hybrid Deployment,

32
00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:03.549
Limitations of AWS Route 53 Integration,
Microsoft Azure Integration,

33
00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:09.405
Google Cloud Platform Integration,
Cloud Forwarders and prerequisites,

34
00:02:09.405 --> 00:02:15.070
Discovering Cloud Forwarder Endpoints,
Limitations of Universal DDI;

35
00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:19.582
AWS Integrate VPC IPAM with
Infoblox and What's New Nov.

36
00:02:19.582 --> 00:02:26.373
17, 2025; What's New in Universal DDI for
FedRAMP; Universal Asset Insights AWS,

37
00:02:26.373 --> 00:02:34.940
Azure, GCP discovery pages;
FedRAMP Marketplace FR2017257053.
